# issue: none
# notes: Two patterns that share no variable multiply their rows by a product, which the compiler refuses with `T81` at the second
# notes: unless every component but one is pinned to one row by a `@key` equality in `where`: the fix joins them through the triple
# notes: one edge type writes between them, or writes the intended product as a named relation; nothing executes.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Person {
    handle: String @key
    name: String
}
node Company {
    slug: String @key
    name: String
}
node Collection {
    slug: String @key
}
edge WorksAt: Person -> Company @card(0..1)

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"handle":"ada","name":"Ada"}}
{"type":"Company","data":{"slug":"acme","name":"Acme"}}
{"type":"Collection","data":{"slug":"papers"}}

--- query
query staff() { match { $c: Company, $p: Person } return { $p.name, $c.name } }

--- expect error: type error: T81: `$p: Person` shares no variable with `$c: Company`, so the pattern multiplies their rows by a product; a product is written only when every component but one is pinned to one row by a `@key` equality in `where`

--- query
query shelved() { match { $p: Person, $s: Collection } where $p.name = "Ada" return { $p.name, $s.slug } }

--- expect error: type error: T81: `$s: Collection` shares no variable with `$p: Person`, so the pattern multiplies their rows by a product; a product is written only when every component but one is pinned to one row by a `@key` equality in `where`
